-- title:
--   Power-series presentation of 𝒪[prodᵢℤ/p^{kᵢ}]
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative noetherian local ring that is complete and separated for the adic topology of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, let $p$ be a prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ (the image of $p$ under the canonical map $\mathbb N \to \mathcal O$), let $r$ be a natural number and let $k : \mathrm{Fin}\ r \to \mathbb N$ be arbitrary. Write $\Delta = \prod_{i \in \mathrm{Fin}\ r} \mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb Z/p^{k_i})$ and, for each $i$, let $\delta_i \in \Delta$ be the tuple whose $i$-th coordinate is the multiplicative copy of $1 \in \mathbb Z/p^{k_i}$ and whose other coordinates are trivial. The assertion is that there exists an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\theta$ from the formal power series ring $\mathcal O[[X_i : i \in \mathrm{Fin}\ r]]$ to the group algebra $\mathcal O[\Delta]$ with the following four properties: $\theta(X_i) = [\delta_i] - 1$ for every $i$; $\theta$ is surjective; the kernel of $\theta$ is exactly the ideal generated by the elements $(1 + X_i)^{p^{k_i}} - 1$ for $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\ r$; and $\theta$ is compatible with augmentations, in that for every power series $f$ the counit of the group-algebra bialgebra applied to $\theta(f)$ equals the constant coefficient of $f$.
--
--   This is the standard dictionary $\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]/\big((1+X_i)^{p^{k_i}}-1\big)_i \cong \mathcal O[\Delta]$ for a finite abelian $p$-group $\Delta = \prod_i \mathbb Z/p^{k_i}$ over a complete noetherian local base, stated as the existence of a presentation map rather than as an isomorphism. It is used in the Taylor–Wiles patching apparatus, where the diamond rings $\mathcal O[\Delta]$ are regarded as quotients of a fixed power series ring, and is cited by [`Algebra.nonempty_patchingDatum_of_levelData`](thm.html#Algebra.nonempty_patchingDatum_of_levelData).
